      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MOOSE (3) is the one to beat after starting odds-on and finishing fourth on debut in a 3yo+ Maiden at this track, beaten two and a half lengths after covering ground and still picking up nicely from a mile back in the run. Can sit closer this time from an inside draw and he can land the knockout blow with the benefit of the debut run under his belt. LUNARIS (8) is the main danger, having made solid late ground when fifth at this venue last start and she had a genuine hold-up from the 175m. Pike sticks with her again today and she can run over the top. TEX 'N' CEE (1) stuck on well when unable to reel in a good winner last start at Bunbury. Out to 1400m doesn't look an issue, and with his racing pattern, he'll be in this for a very long way. THE STALAGMITE (4) was plain when last at Northam, but his debut fourth at this track was solid. Expecting a better run this time. FROSTED WARRIOR (2) is next best stepping out in distance.",
